## Reduce Registry modal loading waits

Context: Opening the Registry modal started another Browse request even when
the page-load request had just completed or remained in flight. Bridges did
not begin loading until its tab was selected, and rapid open/switch actions
could start duplicate aggregation requests.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/registry/js/registry.js
   Added in-flight deduplication and a 15-second freshness window for Browse,
   deduplicated Bridges loads, prefetched Bridges on modal open, preserved
   forced Refresh behavior, and invalidated prefetched Bridges after domain
   mutations.
2. src/front/static/global/js/registry-modal.js
   Identified modal-originated section events so Registry loading can prefetch
   only for the popup interaction.
3. tests/units/front/test_registry_modal_loading.py
   Added contracts for modal event sourcing, Browse caching, Bridges prefetch
   deduplication, explicit refreshes, and mutation invalidation.
4. tests/units/front/test_registry_backend_column.py
   Updated the Backend-column contract for the extracted internal Browse
   loader.
5. docs/user-guide.md
   Documented short-lived Browse reuse, background Bridges loading, and
   explicit Refresh behavior.

